{"name":"Candlestick Point","hex":"#fff1d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candlestick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A holder with a socket or spike for a candle.","A gymnastics move in which the legs are pointed vertically upward."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To catch on fire, so that the chute resembles a tapered candle with a flame on top.","To analyze stock behavior using Japanese candlestick charts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candlestick"},{"term":"point","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small dot or mark.\nSomething tiny, as a pinprick; a very small mark. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something tiny, as a pinprick; a very small mark. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Point taken; understood; got it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/point"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candlestick Point State Recreation Area","blocks":[{"text":"Candlestick Point State Recreation Area is a state park unit of California, United States, providing an urban protected area on San Francisco Bay. The park is located at the southeastern tip of San Francisco immediately south of Hunters Point and 2 miles (3.2 km) north of Sierra Point in Brisbane. This 170-acre (69 ha) landfilled area was intended to be used during World War II as a shipyard by the United States Navy. However it was abandoned as the war ended. Without government controls, the area was used by nearby residences as a garbage dump. In 1973 the California State Legislature purchased the land with US$10 million and in 1977 voted to turn this area into a California State Park. After the designation Candlestick became the first urban recreation area in the state. To this day Candlestick remains as a major recreation area in San Francisco, offering a wide view of the bay. The park features various picnic areas, two fishing piers, fitness courses as well as hiking trails. This park is also a popular area for windsurfing due to strong and regular winds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Candlestick_Point_Park5.jpg/330px-Candlestick_Point_Park5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_Point_State_Recreation_Area","wikidata":"Q5031998"},{"title":"Candlestick","blocks":[{"text":"A candlestick is a device used to hold a candle upright in place. Most candlesticks have a cup, a spike, or both to secure the candle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Candlestick_%28one_of_a_set_of_eight%29_MET_DP-13265-131.jpg/330px-Candlestick_%28one_of_a_set_of_eight%29_MET_DP-13265-131.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick","wikidata":"Q151771"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gloucester_candlestick.jpg/500px-Gloucester_candlestick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gloucester_candlestick.jpg/500px-Gloucester_candlestick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 12th-century Gloucester Candlestick, noted for its intricate Romanesque design.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGloucester_candlestick.jpg"}],"sounds":{"candlestick":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-candlestick.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-candlestick.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-candlestick.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/27/LL-Q1